# portal 1.03 patch 25 — a row belongs to its owner
#
# 22 made each mode read its own source, and the leak survived: the owner switched to 'portal
# network' with the portal closed and again read the child's names. Two things made that
# possible, and both are in `portalShownRows`:
#
#   1. `held` was one Group, not one per owner. The simple portal's rows become `live`, then
#      `held`; the switch to the network mode makes `live` null (the engine is not running), so
#      the next answer was `held` — the child's group, drawn under 'Сеть порталов'.
#   2. `live` was not checked against the owner. The engine's groups stay in memory after the
#      engine stops, so they still answered as `live` in the simple portal — and the child's
#      servers answered as `live` in the network mode. The vivo's record showed both modes
#      claiming `source=live` while `phase=Off`.
#
# Now:
#   * `live` counts only when its owner is the mode's: engine groups when the mode is rule and
#     the engine is the Active owner of the tunnel, the child's servers when the mode is global
#     and the child is (`portalStatusProvider` reads the record's own `Active` + owner);
#   * `held` is kept per owner (`_heldEngine` / `_heldChild`), and a mode reads only its own;
#   * the order stands: live(own) -> held(own) -> engine `cache` / profile `proxies:` (rule) or
#     the profile's Xray servers (global) -> honest empty (`source=none`);
#   * the transition line names the owner and the rows, so a wrong list is visible:
#
#     kind=switch phase=list duration_ms=41 from=Xray to=Mihomo mode=rule owner=engine
#       source=live rows=28 names=VPN - Main | 🇫🇮 Финляндия 01 | ...
#
# A closed portal has no live answer in either mode: the network mode draws its own document
# (`cache` / `profile`), the simple portal its own servers (`servers`), and the line says which.
